-- check/good (project): a cross-module alias is TRANSPARENT to dispatch.
--
-- `docs/design/static-dispatch-spike.md` §1.2, §6.3 and §11 say an alias
-- declared in another module is `no_methods_on_shape` on the branch, because
-- looking it through would need `Interface.alias_body`, which `checker.md`
-- §7 records as not implemented. That is a SPEC DEFECT: the interface's own
-- `alias` term already carries the expansion (`Interface.Term.Tag.alias`,
-- "an `extra` range whose last word is the expansion"), so `store.resolved`
-- looks a cross-module alias through exactly as it looks a same-module one
-- through, and no new interface field is needed.
--
-- So `==` on an imported `Point` derives over the record shape (§9.2) and
-- `p.x` is the ordinary field access it always was. This fixture pins the
-- behaviour the code has; §11's row overstates the limit.
import Lib exposing (Point, origin)


pub same : Point, Point -> Bool
same a b =
    a == b


pub atOrigin : Point -> Bool
atOrigin p =
    p == origin
